  <section class="py-24 lg:py-32 px-6 bg-beige-50 min-h-screen">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/en/blog/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-charcoal-400 hover:text-sage-500 text-sm mb-10">← Back to Blog</a>
      <article class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg border border-beige-200 p-8 md:p-12">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-serif font-bold text-charcoal-900 mb-3">A Week Inside Our Guangzhou Factory</h1>
        <p class="text-charcoal-400 text-sm mb-8">2026-10-04 · Jeff · 5 min read</p>
        <div class="text-charcoal-700 leading-relaxed space-y-5">
          <p>Monday morning, 8:30 AM, Zengcheng district, Guangzhou. The cutting floor is already running — our six automated lines start before the office does. I walk through with the QC lead to check the week's color matches against approved samples. This is where your leather starts: not in a catalog, but on a table, under light, next to the signed sample.</p>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-charcoal-900 pt-2">Tuesday — color day</h2>
          <p>Color matching is the most underestimated step in upholstery leather. A shop in Texas needs a gray that matches a 2019 truck interior that has faded for five years. That's not picking from a chart — that's mixing. Our color room runs custom matches daily; most take one round, some take three.</p>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-charcoal-900 pt-2">Wednesday — cutting and embroidery</h2>
          <p>The digital cutting tables handle model-specific seat cover kits. Watching a headrest panel get cut to a pattern that started as a file from a shop in Phoenix never gets old. Embroidery runs the logos — some weeks it's shop names, some weeks it's a customer's customer.</p>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-charcoal-900 pt-2">Thursday — QC</h2>
          <p>Twelve QC specialists, four checkpoints. Thickness, grain, color against the signed sample, stitching strength. Rolls that don't pass don't ship — they go back. It costs us; it saves you.</p>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-charcoal-900 pt-2">Friday — containers</h2>
          <p>Friday is loading day. Moisture-protected wrapping, batch labels, container loading plans. A container of rolls heading to the US leaves with traceable batch IDs — so if you ever ask me "which batch is my order," there's an answer.</p>
          <p class="border-l-2 border-sage-400 pl-4 italic font-serif text-charcoal-800">People ask how a pastor ends up running export for a leather factory. My answer: the same God I preach about on Sunday is the one I work for on the cutting floor. The standard doesn't change — only the material does.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-10 pt-6 border-t border-beige-200">
          <p class="text-charcoal-600 text-sm mb-4">If you're an upholstery shop that wants a factory that treats your order like it matters — that's literally what this blog is about.</p>
